      "id": 20,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## Node-to-node network tests\n\nOne `network-mesh-probe` pod runs on every node with pod networking, so the tests traverse the Calico pod network and its ECMP multipath routes. Every five minutes each probe tests every other probe pod:\n\n- **Ping** - 4 ICMP echo requests, 200 ms apart. The table shows the average and maximum RTT and packet loss over the selected range.\n- **Upload** - runs a 2-second iperf3 TCP test with 16 parallel streams to the peer and records the receiver-side throughput.\n- **Download** - runs the same iperf3 test in reverse (`-R`) and records the receiver-side throughput.\n\nRows are the node running the test (`source`), columns are the peer (`destination`). Each source has an `avg` and a `max` row; the values are computed over the dashboard time range. Upload tests send data from row to column; download tests send data from column to row. The tests are phase-shifted across nodes, so the full mesh is not saturated at once.\n\nMetrics are scraped from each probe pod's IP on port 9101 by the `network-mesh-probe` PodMonitor. Long-term history is available through the Thanos data source.\n"
      },
      "title": "How this works",
      "type": "text"
    },
